  {
    "function_v0": {
      "doc": "D1: generic settlement primitive \\xe2\\x80\\x94 the shared fund-movement entrypoint\\nfor position close, liquidation seizure, hidden orders, and agentic\\nsettlement. The **calling contract** (an allowlisted settlement authority)\\nhas already verified its own circuit-specific proof; this entrypoint\\nperforms the pool-level effects that only the custody contract can do:\\n\\n1. spend `spent_nullifiers` in the pool's nullifier set (double-spend\\nprotection for any pool notes consumed by the settlement),\\n2. insert `output_commitments` into the pool Merkle tree (re-shielded\\nnotes / new positions become withdrawable via the normal circuits),\\n3. optionally pay `payout_amount` of the pool asset to `payout_recipient`\\n(funds leaving the shield \\xe2\\x80\\x94 e.g. seized collateral to a keeper).\\n\\nTrust model: the pool trusts an allowlisted authority to have verified the\\nsettlement (amounts, nullifiers, commitments) against its circuit. The\\nallowlist is the security boundary \\xe2\\x80\\x94 only admin-approved contracts can move\\nfunds this way. A contract auto-au",
      "name": "execute_settlement",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "doc": "",
          "name": "authority",
          "type_": "address"
        },
        {
          "doc": "",
          "name": "spent_nullifiers",
          "type_": {
            "vec": {
              "element_type": {
                "bytes_n": {
                  "n": 32
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "doc": "",
          "name": "output_commitments",
          "type_": {
            "vec": {
              "element_type": {
                "bytes_n": {
                  "n": 32
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "doc": "",
          "name": "payout_recipient",
          "type_": {
            "option": {
              "value_type": "address"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "doc": "",
          "name": "payout_amount",
          "type_": "i128"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "result": {
            "ok_type": "void",
            "error_type": "error"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  },
